      "content": "Yes, there are a few subtle misconfigurations that can trigger similar symptoms without being a pure RAM shortage. You should verify that your system in the host has enough available physical RAM and check the kubelet configuration (`--sysctl`, `--oom-score-adjust`) to ensure it isn't overriding the container's limits. Additionally, confirm that the pod isn't stuck in an infinite loop of container restarts where syscalls are lagging and consuming the kernel thread limits, effectively starving the process of resources even if the logical memory limit appears correct.",
